//! The `mask` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS)
//! [shorthand](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Cascade/Shorthand_properties)
//! property hides an element (partially or fully) by masking or clipping a specified area of the
//! image. It is a shorthand for all the [`mask-*`](#constituent_properties) properties. The property
//! accepts one or more comma-separated values, where each value corresponds to a
//! [`<mask-layer>`](#mask-layer).
//!
//! Initial: mask-image: none; mask-mode: match-source; mask-repeat: repeat; mask-position: 0% 0%;
//! mask-clip: border-box; mask-origin: border-box; mask-size: auto; mask-composite: add. Inherited:
//! no.
//! Percentages: mask-position: refer to size of mask painting area minus size of mask layer image
//! (see the text for `background-position`).
//!
//! Grammar: <mask-layer>#
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-masking-1/#propdef-mask
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Additional value descriptions: Microsoft (MIT).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

